meta {
  name: Artifacts - Update Access
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/:workspace/artifacts/:artifact/access
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  workspace: {{workspaceId}}
  artifact: {{artifactId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "general_access": "organization"
  }
}

docs {
  Sets the sharing tier for every version in the artifact's group — General
  Access in Gumloop's terms. Requires `artifact.view`, and only the
  artifact's creator or someone with `artifact.manage` may call it.

  `general_access` is one of:
  - `restricted` — only the creator and users explicitly added via
    `Artifacts - Add Share` can see it (default for a new artifact).
  - `organization` — any workspace member with `artifact.view` can see it.
  - `anyone` — same visibility as `organization` in this app; there is no
    anonymous/public request path, so these two are equivalent here.

  A new version created after this (re-export or re-upload of the same
  group) inherits the group's current `general_access` rather than
  resetting to `restricted`.

  Response is wrapped: `{ success, statusCode, message, data: { artifact } }`.
}
